Short:        Print to network PDF printers, IPP
Uploader:     (We fill this in at upload time)
Author:       AmiCradle Team
Type:         text/print
Version:      0.3
Requires:     bsdsocket.library (GFOpenSocket, Roadshow, AmiTCP or Miami);
              for IPPS, gfopentls.library (GFOpenTLS)
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0
Distribution: Aminet

GFOpenPrint prints from AmigaOS to the printers on your network that take PDF
documents over IPP, and saves documents as PDF files on the Amiga.

- IPPS (encrypted IPP) through gfopentls.library (GFOpenTLS): a printer's own
  certificate is trusted once, by asking, and remembered by its fingerprint.

- GFOpenPrint: one Print window for any document, with printer, copies, range,
  paper and orientation.
- GFOpenView: opens whatever a datatype reads (pictures, text, AmigaGuide,
  documents, sounds, animations), lays pictures out on the page and hands
  them to the Print window. It takes MultiView's command line and ARexx
  commands, so GFOpenUp installs it as SYS:Utilities/MultiView.
- Printers and Queue: finds the printers on the network (DNS-SD/mDNS), keeps
  the ones you use, and shows the print queue.
- A printer driver and oapspool.device, so any program that prints through
  printer.device can print through GFOpenPrint, with a spooler that starts with
  Workbench.
- An Installer script; files of the old name are moved to SYS:Storage, not
  deleted.

All windows are GadTools and adapt to the screen's font. GFOpenPrint and
GFOpenView were called OpenAmigaPrint and OpenAmigaView until October 2026.

